WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Paul Bettany.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.237
Your costar, Jeremy Pope,

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.805
an incredibly talented actor
as well.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.408
Does he get the sense you think
this whole thing is a nightmare

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.010
or --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.612
You know, the truth
is working with Jeremy,

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.548
we've been doing this in
different iterations

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.416
with the film
and we did it in London.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.820
It -- He -- It --
Working with Jeremy

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.324
is as close as you can get
to flying in your dreams.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.127
It's just, when you're tired and
you don't want to do the show,

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.195
he comes on
and I look at him and he's --

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.396
he's just extraordinary.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.965
It's been a real privilege
to work with him.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.134
The kid's a genius.
-That's fantastic.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:36.936
Another collaboration,

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.404
you're coming up
on a 20-year anniversary.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.139
-Oh, yeah.
-You and your beautiful

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.640
charming wife,
Jennifer Connelly,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.509
January 1st, I guess...
-Yes.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:45.344
-...is 20 years.
Congratulations.

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.313
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.915
-20 years.
-Wow.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.016
-Yeah, which in Hollywood years
is like --

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:53.485
-Hollywood years, yeah.
-Like 80.

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:55.154
-It's very impressive.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.856
And yet I would imagine,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.592
due to your schedule,
you really can't do much, right?

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.695
With your theater schedule?
-Oh, God, that's true, yeah.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.366
No, yeah.
Yes, this is an entire disaster.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.934
[ Laughter ]
They make you work.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.137
They make you work on,
like, holidays and stuff.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.739
-Yeah.
-Like lure a first responder

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.207
or something.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.774
The whole thing's ridiculous.

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:19.412
You know, it's been --

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.013
it's been 20 --
it's been 20 years.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.248
We've -- It's been wonderful,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.850
and we've really
got to know each other.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.251
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.519
Now.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.256
And -- You know, the amazing
thing about it is --

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.524
How long have you been married?

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.992
-Coming up on 10.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.261
-Okay, well -- yeah.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.662
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.298
-I think -- I think
in like three years.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.832
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, but not --

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.101
not as good as 20.
-No, no.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.169
Of course not.
-Whatever.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:47.073
Anyway, the thing
that's amazing about it,

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.441
being married 20 years,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:53.212
is that my wife is still
utterly fascinated by me.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.648
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, she finds me fascinating.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.617
And I can tell.
You know, we'll be at --

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.986
you know, having dinner
or whatever,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.988
I'll be talking
about the news or my career.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.422
Mostly my career.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:04.623
[ Light laughter ]
-Obviously.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.327
And she is sometimes
so fascinated

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.529
that she takes her food and
she eats it in the other room.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:14.600
[ Laughter ]
Presumably to ruminate

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.636
on all the amazing things
I just --

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.171
-Yeah, just like unpack
everything you just told her.

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:20.740
-Right.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.642
So that's -- that's what being
married for 20 years feels like.

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:25.111
-That's really lovely.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:28.781
You -- You know, obviously you
have a lot of holiday tourists

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.616
that I'm assuming are in town
to come see your show,

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.685
but you also had the privilege
of some high schoolers

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.121
came to see your show.
-Yes, yes.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.490
I -- What a feral bunch.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.891
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.427
They -- They were -- Yeah.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.295
So we did this -- So we --

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.465
Yeah, we did this show for --
for schoolkids.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.633
And --

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.901
-So you know,
this is the schoolkids day.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:49.869
-Yes.
-You're prepared in advance.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:50.937
Okay.
-Yes.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.005
And they laugh
every time you swear.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.508
They laugh -- Then there's
this moment in the show

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:59.311
where I have to
take my shirt off.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:02.848
Right?
And they lost their [bleep].

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:05.751
[ Laughter ]
I mean, just lost their [bleep].

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:09.588
And then what happened
was Jeremy Pope

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.324
then takes his shirt off.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:14.894
And I noticed
they wolf whistled for him.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.963
-So it was like funny
when your shirt came off.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.497
-Yeah, no,
that's exactly the point.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:21.467
Yeah, they found it hilarious
when I took my shirt off.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.402
And then it was just quiet

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.404
except for endless wolf
whistles.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:27.507
So this whole process

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.209
of doing this on Broadway
is just humiliating.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.243
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.778
It's been --
frankly, it's been --

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:34.847
You know, I think it's been
a hard year for everybody,

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.682
but mostly me.
-Yeah, yeah. I think --

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.752
I think, you know, everybody's
New Year's resolution

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:43.222
should be hoping
that you have a better 2023.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.924
-I'm sure that's already
what they're thinking.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:48.261
-You know what, I'm sorry,
I hate to continue

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.262
with a hammer on the things
that have gone wrong for you,

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:53.966
but Jennifer was in
"Top Gun: Maverick"

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.735
which has done very well
at the box office.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.503
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:02.108
And it is now -- it is now the
sixth highest grossing movie.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.310
And in order to go from seventh
to sixth,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.179
it passed "Avengers:
Infinity War" which you were in.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.981
[ Laughter ]
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:11.583
-Now you, by with way,
you posted this and did say,

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:12.885
if we can come over here,

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.120
"I'm just never going to live
this down in the house."

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.923
Is that --
-That's true.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.925
-Is she really just sort of
taking a victory lap on this?

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.561
-Yes, and I'm allowing her to,

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.864
because what she doesn't know,
it's just a lull in hostilities.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.165
-Right.
-I have texted Kevin Feige.

00:04:27.165 --> 00:04:28.234
He says, "I'm on it."

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.468
[ Light laughter ]
-Right.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.637
-"We're going to take back
the mantle for you."

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.973
-There's more "Avengers" stuff
coming.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.340
-Oh, yeah.
-All you have to do is be in it

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.742
for a little bit
for it to count.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.711
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.112
Well, that's a fair point.

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:43.249
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.750
I cannot wait to see the show.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.552
And have a happy new year
and happy anniversary.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.521
Always a pleasure.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.023
[ Cheers and applause ]
Paul Bettany, everybody.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:53.159
"The Collaboration" opens
December 20th

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:56.195
at Manhattan Theatre Club,
Samuel J. Friedman Theatre.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.397
For more information, go to
manhattantheatreclub.com.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:04:59.766
We'll be right back
with Lily Collins.

